WEBVTT

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.070
Here...

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.740
Get on my shoulders.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:18.730
Oof.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:39.760
<i>That's how it always starts...</i>
<i>under the azure sky</i>

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:46.930
<i>After making a vow,</i>
<i>I now set off</i>

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:06.050
<i>Yeah, the desert glitters with a golden hue</i>
<i>(The wind is scorching)</i>

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:12.390
<i>I'm searching for a diamond flower</i>
<i>(I keep on wandering)</i>

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:18.730
<i>Now, for the first time in my life,</i>

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:25.070
<i>I live for someone else</i>

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:31.580
<i>There's something</i>
<i>I wanna protect</i>

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:38.080
<i>I'll never,</i>
<i>ever lose it again</i>

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.090
<i>Resound,</i>
<i>my heartbeat!</i>

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:51.080
<i>A heartbeat smaller and fragile,</i>
<i>but tougher than anyone's.</i>

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:07.700
"Badly Wounded Cat"

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:11.050
You bastard, I'll make
you pay for this!!

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:14.380
Train... You still don't get it?

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:18.050
That woman was a witch
who was leading you astray.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.390
You bastard...

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:24.090
I swear I'll make you
pay for this!!

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.740
That look!

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.730
That look in your eyes!

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.360
So what do you think?
Aren't they pretty?

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:06.700
It looks as if flowers
are blossoming in the sky.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.370
<i>Tamaya</i>!!

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.700
What's that?

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:12.370
That's what you say
when fireworks are going off.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.050
<i>Tagaya</i>!!

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.040
That's a <i>Rakugo</i> comedy!

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.060
<i>Tamaya</i>!!

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.390
No!

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:35.300
Hey, it's not "no",
it's "<i>Tamaya</i>", right?

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.070
What's the matter?

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:42.070
The smell... of blood...

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:43.070
Huh?

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.070
I'm going...

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.410
--Where to?
--The sea...

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.080
Th- the sea!?

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.080
--That way...
--That way? Umm...

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.980
--Hurry up!
--Uhh... Okay, okay!

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:02.060
The fireworks are pretty,
aren't they!?

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:06.360
Oh? What's the matter?

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.350
You're crying...

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:13.600
You really are funny,
Train-<i>kun</i>!

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:17.370
Oh? Me, too...

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.040
It can't be helped, right?

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.710
'Cause fireworks are so pretty!

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:25.710
See? Isn't this pretty?

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:28.720
Don't worry...
Your eyes are...

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:31.550
as pretty as fireworks...

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.000
You're... Torneo's...

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:04.690
It's not "he came to life",
it's "he came to", right, Eve?

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:07.690
Hey! How're you feeling?

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:10.360
You're that sweeper...
What are you doing here?

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:13.130
This is my house...
or rather, it's my hideout.

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:14.360
Hideout?

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:18.030
What a shock that was! When we went
to the pier like Eve suggested,

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:20.190
we saw a tanker in flames...

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:28.040
Hey! Don't get close!

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:31.050
Eve! It's dangerous!

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:32.710
I smell blood...

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:36.380
Ow, ow! Eve! If we go any further,
we could really get hurt!

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:39.720
That way...

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:43.390
How far are you gonna go, Eve!?

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:44.590
There he is!

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:57.070
So, after this and that, we rescued you
from the flames of the exploding tanker.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.070
Be thankful.

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.340
Exploding...

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.340
Where's Saya!?

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.340
Saya?

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:04.680
She was wearing a <i>yukata</i>!

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:08.680
<i>Yukata</i>?
We didn't see her.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.850
Was she with you?

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:19.360
I'm sorry, but either way, I don't
think she'd survive in that explosion.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:23.030
How long... was I asleep?

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:25.370
A week.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:27.030
A week...

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:31.770
But I changed my mind about you.

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:35.040
After all, in the middle of all that,
you protected those kids to the end.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.380
That's not something
just anyone could do.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:38.710
Kids?

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:42.720
Don't worry. I heard that
all three of them are just fine.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:44.310
I don't remember.

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:51.730
You're hungry, aren't you?

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:55.730
Now, don't hold back!
Eat to your heart's content!

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:59.730
What's the matter? If you don't eat,
you won't get better.

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:02.670
Where's my gun?

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:07.340
Eve, give it to him.

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:10.400
He still smells of blood...

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:21.360
Please give this to the man in black
and say, "thanks for saving us!"

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.360
So, I'll give this to you.

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:26.880
But I won't give you
the gun back.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:42.040
Well, we all ended up living under
the same roof. This must be fate.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:43.980
In any case,
why don't we be friends?

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.390
Don't be so edgy.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:59.060
He's an injured man.

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:03.660
Be nice to him, at least
until he gets better.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:06.000
But he's...

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.660
An assassin, you mean?

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:12.540
But he didn't shoot you.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:20.510
So, his gun... give it
back to him, will you?

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:28.360
Anyway, these days you've always
got your nose in a book...

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:29.690
I want to know...

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:32.360
You want to know...
about what?

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:33.690
A lot of things...

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:36.030
A lot of things?

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:40.370
Because I had been
taught only one thing...

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.430
I see...

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:48.040
So, what have you learned?

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:52.050
Let's see, "A Guide to Martial Arts"
and "Three Minute Cooking"...

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:55.380
"Cherry Blossom Viewing from
A Row House" and "Camels' Humps"...

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:57.720
<i>"Tagaya</i>"!

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:01.320
And, what you're
perusing right now is...

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:02.660
Aesop...

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:04.330
Aesop?

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:07.330
It's a fable.
Annette gave it to me.

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:10.330
That's a mean-looking cat.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:14.000
It's a story about putting
a bell on a bad cat's neck.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.340
A bell... on a cat's neck?

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:20.330
Right. They put a bell
on a bad cat's neck.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:38.690
Well, then, I'm going
grocery shopping for dinner,

00:09:38.690 --> 00:09:40.680
so, stay home with him.

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:44.030
Hey, don't give me that look.

00:09:44.030 --> 00:09:46.030
We can't go leaving
an injured man alone, right?

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:49.040
I'll get you something.
What do you want?

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.030
A book!

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:12.060
It's from the guest over there.

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:13.730
Oh?

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:16.400
The name of this
cocktail is "Fate".

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:19.400
It's a suitable name
for our meeting...

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:20.400
Don't you think?

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.070
Yeah...

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:24.410
You have beautiful eyes...

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:27.410
To your beautiful eyes!

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:28.930
Jenos-<i>sama...</i>

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:33.750
Belze is-?

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:37.080
I'm sorry, but I have to go.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:39.750
My name?

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:43.950
Ask the god of "Fate"
who brought you and I together...

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:47.950
Who's going to pay
for this "Fate"?

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.380
Welcome!

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:14.050
Coffee... Make it hot and strong,
like you'd get at a mountain cottage...

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:17.730
Okay, and put it on
your tab as usual, right?

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:19.390
That's right...

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:21.120
Wha-!? How!?

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:28.070
So, what's Rins up to?

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:31.070
She left town. She said
that she got a job.

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:33.740
She told me she'd make
a lot of money this time.

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:35.740
Good to hear
that she's all right.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:37.750
Yeah...

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:41.420
Anyway, about that explosion
at the pier the other day...

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:43.750
Oh, the one on the night
of the festival...

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:45.750
Have you heard
anything about it?

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:47.520
According to the
official announcement,

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:51.320
fireworks supposedly caused
the tanker to catch fire, but...

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:54.430
But the truth is?

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:56.100
I don't know.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:12:01.040
I heard that three kids were caught
in the explosion and got light burns,

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:04.040
but they seem
to remember nothing...

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:05.370
Nothing?

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:10.710
Listen, I don't want you to mention
the man in black to anyone.

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:11.380
Got it!

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:12.710
I won't tell anyone!

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:14.050
Me neither!

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:17.050
I see...
That's good...

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:19.050
You look like
you know something.

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:21.720
Not really...

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:24.390
Oh well...
Anyway, where's Eve?

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:27.390
Yeah, she's reading
picture books at my hideout.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:30.060
Sounds like she's doing fine.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.400
Yeah, thanks.

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:34.400
But don't let your guard down.

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:38.070
I heard that Chronos guys
are snooping around everywhere.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:41.740
Man, those guys
sure are persistent...

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.080
Ouch!
Ow, ow, ouch!!

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:49.080
Torneo's bio-weapon?

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:53.750
It was No. XIII's mission,
but I want you to take it over.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:57.420
Don't tell me Black Cat failed...

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:00.690
He left Chronos and disappeared.

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:03.530
There was a report that he died
in that explosion at the pier,

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:05.370
but I wouldn't count on it.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:07.030
I see...

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:08.870
Will you take this job?

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:14.040
Thanks.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:17.380
So, why did Black Cat
leave Chronos?

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:20.050
You don't have to know.

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:23.210
If you find him, I'll leave
the matter up to you.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:28.060
What a bad road!

00:13:28.060 --> 00:13:29.720
Please be patient.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:30.720
I've got information

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:33.660
that the bio-weapon was definitely
brought to somewhere around here.

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:39.400
Why do you keep fighting!?

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:41.070
I myself don't know why,

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:43.400
but once we get in a robot,
we have no choice but to fight, right!?

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:46.070
Yeah, it's true that when we,
children, get in a robot,

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:49.740
we all become war victims
for some reason!!

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:52.080
Move.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.980
I can't see the TV!

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:58.090
I'm going to...
put a bell...

00:13:58.090 --> 00:13:59.420
Huh?

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:03.360
I'm going to put a bell
on a bad cat's neck

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:07.030
so that he won't
be dangerous anymore...

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:09.700
This is why I say
the federation military is-!

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:12.170
I don't understand
what you're saying at all!

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:15.700
Why are things
turning out like this!?

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:17.370
This is what war is!!

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.530
Giga-ton Punch!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:27.380
How can you say
"put a bell on a bad cat"?

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:30.040
You tried to kill me, too.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.390
You're an assassin, too.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:49.060
I don't wanna wage war
in a robot any more!!

00:14:58.750 --> 00:14:59.750
I'm home!

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:04.350
Eve, I bought a book for you.
"Art of Calligraphy is the Stray"...

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:08.690
Hey, where did Eve go?

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:10.360
What!?

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:11.690
Idiot!

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:14.030
That's her...

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:15.360
What?

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:20.030
Are you saying that little lady
is the bio-weapon that Torneo developed?

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:22.370
Yes. It's no mistake.

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:31.710
I don't know
what happened to you.

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:34.720
If you don't open up to us,
that's okay, too.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:39.050
But, it was Eve who found you
at that explosion site,

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:43.720
and who looked after you all that
time you were in bed for a week.

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:47.060
Listen up. If you say
something to hurt her again,

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:50.290
I'll make you pay for it,
even if you're injured.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:01.670
You're an assassin, too.

00:16:08.350 --> 00:16:11.020
Good evening...

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:12.690
...mademoiselle.

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:17.020
Hey! Where are you!? Eve!!

00:16:19.030 --> 00:16:21.720
What's your name,
mademoiselle?

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:29.040
Now, now, what are you
backing away for?

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:31.710
Did you come to capture me?

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:34.470
No. I came to escort you.

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:41.720
Jenos-<i>sama,</i>
please be careful.

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:44.050
She's a monster.

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:46.390
Watch what you say.

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:49.060
It's rude to the lady.

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:51.060
Now...

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:52.720
Let's go...

00:16:54.060 --> 00:16:55.060
...mademoiselle.

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:57.730
I'm not... going...

00:16:57.730 --> 00:17:01.670
What a dilemma. I promised
that I'd bring you with me...

00:17:01.670 --> 00:17:03.340
No...

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:06.670
Please...
Come with me...

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:12.680
You're it.

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:14.350
You're an assassin, too.

00:17:14.350 --> 00:17:16.020
No!!!

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:17.010
Whoa!

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:21.520
So, that's the power
of nanomachines!

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:28.030
You damn monster!

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:29.690
Game over, mademoiselle!

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:38.040
I'm sorry for getting
rough with you.

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:40.710
If you come with me
without a fight,

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:43.700
I'll make it so that
the pain won't be any worse.

00:17:45.050 --> 00:17:46.040
No!!

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:53.950
This thread is made
of orichalcum.

00:17:57.060 --> 00:18:00.990
Now, please...
Say you'll come with me...

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:02.390
Or else...

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:07.830
N- no!

00:18:10.670 --> 00:18:12.000
Ouch!!

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:17.010
A bell?

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:18.600
Ow, ow, ow...

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:31.690
What a surprise!

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:35.360
I never thought I'd be able to see
Black Cat in a place like this.

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:38.370
You must be one
of the Numbers...

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:43.040
That's right! I'm No. VII,
Jenos Hazard.

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:45.040
Never heard of you...

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:48.380
Just as expected of No. XIII,
the bringer of bad luck,

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:50.710
You keep your cool!

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:53.710
I'm no longer
one of the Numbers!

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:56.380
I'm a stray cat
who does as he pleases!

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:58.050
A stray cat, huh?

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:02.320
Belze'll probably be happy
if I bring you to Chronos,

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.810
along with the bio-weapon
mademoiselle.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:10.330
Let's get something straight.
She isn't a weapon.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:11.670
She's a human!

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.330
This is also
part of my mission!

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:25.170
Black Cat!!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.350
That's wishful
thinking, Black Cat!

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:33.250
Even if you fire three bullets,
it's not gonna beat my Excellion.

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:39.360
Damn!

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:44.700
Sorry, but my Hades
is also "orichalcum made".

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.930
Eve, I'll leave
the rest to you!

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:53.710
What!?
Chronos came!?

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.040
But I beat them up.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:59.050
Dummy! He purposely pretended
that he was knocked out.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:00.080
What?

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:02.550
There's no way one of the Numbers
would be knocked unconscious

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.050
just by being hit with a hammer.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:08.060
So, why are you guys
having dinner together,

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:11.390
while I was out looking all over
for Eve for three and a half long hours?

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:12.390
Because I was starving...

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:13.830
Because I was hungry...

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:16.060
Jenos-<i>sama...</i>

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.730
Forget about
what happened tonight.

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:20.070
--But...
--Forget it!

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:22.400
U- understood.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.740
How many miles do we
have left to reach the town?

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:27.740
20 miles...

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:31.410
Thanks to Black Cat,
our car was trashed!

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:32.750
That was because you...

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:34.080
Shut up!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.080
What shall we report
to Belze-<i>sama</i>?

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:40.090
This matter was left to me.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:42.090
So, I'll decide
what we're gonna do.

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:44.760
Yes...

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:48.430
A stray cat who does
as he pleases, huh?

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.100
We're already leaving?

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:54.430
If we stay here, Chronos could
come back any time, right!?

00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:57.440
You don't need
to worry about that...

00:20:57.440 --> 00:21:00.710
By the way, what's up
with that bell on your neck?

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:03.040
Oh, yeah, it's slick, isn't it?

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:07.710
Hmm... But I feel like
I've seen that bell somewhere...

00:21:15.390 --> 00:21:20.390
Then, you're saying that Creed
used some uncanny power?

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:23.060
Yes. According to Nizer...

00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:29.240
--Could it be Tao?
--Very possibly.

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:32.740
I also crossed swords with a man
who called himself a Taoist.

00:21:32.740 --> 00:21:35.580
However, those with
the power of the Tao

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:40.410
were supposed to be eradicated
in the war 20 years ago.

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:44.750
Are the survivors of the "Itairiku War"
trying to cause an uproar?

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:48.090
But, why can Creed
use the power of the Tao?

00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:52.430
It seems that an ill wind
is blowing, doesn't it?

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:55.430
The Council of Elders
is also concerned.

00:21:55.430 --> 00:22:01.030
They ordered us to focus on investigating
Creed and the Taoists for now.

00:22:01.030 --> 00:22:05.530
In the meantime, you should
forget about other matters.

00:22:11.440 --> 00:22:16.480
<i>The stars in the night sky</i>
<i>are my tears</i>

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:20.480
<i>Goddess of the moon,</i>
<i>angel of the stars!</i>

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:26.250
<i>Please stop time tonight!</i>

00:22:35.170 --> 00:22:41.170
<i>Please show yourself,</i>
<i>even if just a little</i>

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:46.940
<i>Around the time the first evening star</i>
<i>appears, I hear footsteps approaching</i>

00:22:46.940 --> 00:22:52.850
<i>The only time I can see you</i>
<i>is when the moon is shining</i>

00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:55.850
<i>Please let me dream a little</i>

00:22:55.850 --> 00:22:59.090
<i>'Cause it'll become</i>
<i>an illusion by morning</i>

00:22:59.090 --> 00:23:02.460
<i>Even though I know it,</i>
<i>I still feel lonely</i>

00:23:02.460 --> 00:23:08.130
<i>The stars in the night sky</i>
<i>are my tears</i>

00:23:08.130 --> 00:23:14.140
<i>You held me in your arms</i>
<i>and your passionate lips met mine</i>

00:23:14.140 --> 00:23:17.140
<i>Please don't let go of me</i>

00:23:17.140 --> 00:23:20.480
<i>I'm about to melt in your arms</i>

00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:23.310
<i>But morning is almost here</i>

00:23:23.310 --> 00:23:26.820
<i>Goddess of the moon,</i>
<i>angel of the stars!</i>

00:23:26.820 --> 00:23:33.160
<i>I pray to you,</i>
<i>please stop time</i>

00:23:40.500 --> 00:23:41.000
"Next Episode"

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:42.730
I'm Sven Vollfied.
"Next Episode"

00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:45.400
I'm a cool,
lone-wolf sweeper.

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:51.070
But, why am I, the cool, lone-wolf sweeper,
traveling with two dependents!?

00:23:51.070 --> 00:23:55.750
Damn! A cold wind blows
through my empty wallet...

00:23:55.750 --> 00:23:58.420
Oh well, I guess
I'll work hard.

00:23:58.420 --> 00:24:02.350
Hey, Train! Quit napping
all day and give me a hand!

00:24:02.350 --> 00:24:02.550
Oh, no need
to get up, Eve.

00:24:02.550 --> 00:24:05.460
"Traveling Cat"
Oh, no need
to get up, Eve.
